From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Defer executable stripping to RPM post-processing

The default link rule strips its own output before RPM can collect debug
information. Retain the original link command and every default target;
let the normal RPM scripts produce debug products and strip the binary.
No C source or runtime behavior is changed. Downstream-only, MIT.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -27 +27 @@
-	@strip $@
+	# Final stripping is performed by the RPM packaging scripts.
